# Fundraising partner-facing URLs

## Invariant

Official partner documents, Lookup links, PDFs, and partner emails **always** use `https://www.selpic.com.au`. Never `localhost`, LAN IPs, or `*.vercel.app`.

Lookup is live on production. Do not tell operators to use `http://localhost:…/fundraising/lookup` in partner-facing copy.

## Why this leaked

Admin Documents / sample extras used `window.location.origin`. Generating on `http://localhost:3005` persisted that origin inside `htmlBody`. Lookup then showed:

`Or copy this link: http://localhost:3005/fundraising/lookup?token=…`

`siteBaseUrl()` also followed `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` / `VERCEL_URL`, so local and preview deploys could mint non-public Lookup URLs.

## Required helpers

| Use | Helper |
|-----|--------|
| Lookup / partner docs / partner emails | `buildPartnerFacingLookupUrl` / `getPartnerFacingSiteUrl` (`lib/fundraising/partnerFacingSite.ts`, `lib/publicSiteUrl.ts`) |
| HTML already stored or pasted | `healFundraisingDocumentHtml` / `rewriteHtmlUnsuitableOriginsToPublicSite` |
| Admin-only inbound emails | `siteBaseUrl()` is OK for `/admin/…` links to staff — still heal any HTML that partners can see |

Do **not** use `window.location.origin` or `siteBaseUrl()` for partner Lookup links.

## Cousins to check when touching this

- Admin Documents generate / sample preview / Send / resend
- Welcome pack D2/D4 and renewal D18–D20
- Stored `fundraising_documents.payload.htmlBody` (heal on read + write)
- Lookup dashboard document viewer + PDF download
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3005` in local `.env`
- Vercel Preview `VERCEL_URL`
- Apex `http://selpic.com.au` vs canonical `https://www.selpic.com.au`
- Sample token preview (`samplepreviewtoken…`) — host must still be production; token is preview-only

